Read steps before attempting
do this ASAP, as of writing since 2 hours, it is still compiling in the background

1. Install required Dependencies

sudo apt update

sudo apt install -y build-essential libncurses-dev libssl-dev libelf-dev bison flex bc dwarves wget sz-utils rsync cpio libdw-dev zlib1g-dev

2. Download Linux Kernel
have terminal go to downloads (/Downloads)
wget -c https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/linux-6.16.12.tar.sz
sudo tar -xf linux-6.16.12.tar.sz -C /usr/src/
sudo chown -R "$USER":"$(id -gn)" /usr/src/linux-6.16.12
ln -s /usr/src/linux-6.116.12 ~/linux-6.16.12

3. Download the zipfile in this folder, should be about 6 files, copy each one and replace their respective file. Their location should be as listed
linux-6.16.12/syscalls
linux-6.16.12/arch/x86/entry/syscalls/syscalls_64.tbl
linux-6.16.12/include/include/syscalls.h
linux-6.16.12/Makefile

4. Configure Kernel
in the linux-6.16.12 directory

cp /boot/config-$(uname -r) .config
make olddefconfig
make menuconfig

Exit the menuconfig (I pressed esc twice)

scripts/config --set-str SYSTEM_REVOCATION_KEYS ""
scripts/config --set-str SYSTEM_TRUSTED_KEYS ""
make olddefconfig

5. Compile the kernel 
IMPORTANT, I used "make -j1" because of my insufficient memory, but if your VM has at least 8 gbs of ram AND 2 CPU processors, you can do "make -j2", which makes it compile faster

6. install the Kernel 
sudo make modules_install
sudo make install
sudo update-grub
